Both records refer to an existing diesel deal between the US and Russia, with the actors, action and object all matching. The left record names the Trump administration, with Trump and Putin as principals, and the right says "US and Russia", which is a difference in granularity rather than a conflict. Neither record gives a time or any details of the deal, so nothing indicates two different deals. Both are background references to the same deal.

The risk is that each could point to a different diesel arrangement, but nothing in the evidence suggests that. I judge them equivalent.

